<div class="marketing-page" data-controller="scroll-reveal">
<%= render 'shared/marketing_header' %>

<section class="mkt-hero" style="padding: 4rem 0 5rem;">
  <div class="mkt-inner">
    <span class="mkt-hero__eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem; display: inline-flex;">
      <span class="mkt-hero__eyebrow-dot"></span>
      Last updated: <%= Date.current.strftime("%B %d, %Y") %>
    </span>
    <h1 class="mkt-hero__title" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3.25rem);">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mkt-hero__subtitle" style="max-width: 36rem;">
      I collect the minimum needed to run the hosted site. I don’t sell your data
      and I don’t run analytics on you.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="mkt-section bg-white">
  <div class="mkt-inner--narrow">

    <div class="mkt-highlight-box mkt-highlight-box--blue mkt-reveal" data-scroll-reveal-target="item" style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <strong>The short version:</strong> on peponi.to I store your email, hashed password, and your tasks
      for up to seven days, then I delete them. I don’t track you. On Omarchy local mode,
      tasks never leave that machine. If you self-host, the data lives on your computer, not mine.
    </div>

    <div class="mkt-prose mkt-reveal" data-scroll-reveal-target="item">

      <h2>What I collect on peponi.to</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email and name</strong> — so you can sign in</li>
        <li><strong>Password</strong> — hashed. I cannot see the actual password</li>
        <li><strong>Your pages and tasks</strong> — so the planner works during the hosted week</li>
        <li><strong>A session cookie</strong> — so you stay logged in. Not for tracking</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you use the contact form, I receive whatever you type there.
      </p>
      <p>
        I do not collect analytics, advertising data, or “sign in with Google” profiles.
      </p>

      <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Hosted accounts are deleted after seven days, along with their tasks.
        You can export or delete sooner from Settings.
        People who already paid in the old shop model are not deleted automatically.
      </p>

      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        If email is configured, I use Brevo only to send account mail (welcome, “your week is ending”, password changes).
        I don’t send marketing newsletters.
      </p>

      <h2>Omarchy and self-host</h2>
      <p>
        Local Omarchy mode never sends tasks to peponi.to.
        If you sign in once, I copy existing hosted tasks onto that machine; new work stays there.
        A clone you run yourself stores data in your SQLite file. That is not my server.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This is not aimed at children under 13. I don’t knowingly collect their data.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions: the <%= link_to "contact form", contact_path %>.
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<%= render 'shared/footer' %>
</div>
